      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Satellites require dedicated infrastructure to launch, identify, and communicate with.\n\nBefore anything leaves the ground, every satellite must be assigned a unique frequency using the §3Satellite ID Manager§r. Place the satellite in its right slot to generate a random frequency, then use the left and center slots to copy that frequency onto §6Satellite ID Chips§r or other linked devices such as designators. ID Chips must be prepared in advance. The assigned frequency appears in the item\u0027s tooltip.\n\nSatellites can be launching using a custom rocket or Soyuz-FG.\n\nOnce a satellite is in orbit, a §3Satellite Ground Station§r handles communication. It does not process §dRedstone-over-Radio§r signals directly - it requires an external RoR receiver or transmitter. It connects to one satellite at a time, switched via the appropriate §6Satellite ID Chip§r or an RoR command. RX reads data transmitted down from the satellite; TX sends commands up to it.\n\n§2The Ground Station\u0027s capabilities expand significantly when paired with an §3AUTOCAL§r§2, enabling automated satellite tracking, data processing, and chained multi-satellite logic.",
